! Institutional and civic events are sometimes scheduled to take place on
! the nth (first, second, third, etc.) occurrence of a specified weekday
! (Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, etc.) of each or of a particular month. For
! example, a company may hold a senior management meeting on the second
! Tuesday of each month. American Thanksgiving occurs on the 4th Thursday
! of November each year, while Canadian Thanksgiving occurs on the second
! Monday in October.
! 
! Task
! 
! Write a subroutine/procedure/function/method, or whatever is idiomatic
! in your language, to return the day of the month upon which the nth
! occurrence of a specified weekday occurs in a specified month and year,
! or an appropriate error value if no such instance exists (say, the fifth
! Sunday in a month that lacks one). Use it to show the dates on which
! Canadian and American Thanksgiving will fall for each year in the decade
! 2020 through 2029.
! 
! Related tasks
! 
! - Five weekends
! - Day of the week
! - Find the last Sunday of each month
! - Last Friday of each month


